This is a note to those looking for quick ways to beat the game:  There
are none.

There are indeed ways to play -- and often win -- a slightly different game: 
	Wizard mode
	discovery mode
	Saving backups
	Importing bones files
	Polypiling, etc.

These are all legitimate variants of Nethack and who is to say which is
the correct or right or official version.  Posters delight in posting
cheats, hacks, special techniques, strategies, etc.  There are also
those who like to post false spoilers to confound the naive.  A wand of
wishing on the first level is probably one of these.  Poor, confused
beginners will spend hours poring through the code or the spoiler sheet
or netpostings to find the latest way to avoid having to play the hard
parts of the game.  Meanwhile, certain features of the game (such as,
for example, the way to use a credit card in a store, or the way to make
an offering without an altar, or the way to wrap a weapon bonus so as to
have a - weapon actually behave as a mega +++ weapon) are ignored.

People are certainly free to play whatever variant of the game they
wish.  The free (and worth it at twice the price!) advice of one who
has played Nethack from Version 1.0 is to play by the rules and see if
you can still win.  A glorious death is more fun than a cheating win.

